{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/759423-how-to-weaponize-the-imbued","id":759423,"title":"How to Weaponize the Imbued?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-06T15:21:16-08:00","id":759423,"title":"How to Weaponize the Imbued?","content":"How can other supernaturals, the righteous noble Garou the Majestic lords of the Fae courts, or the Elegant yet sinister Kindred, weaponize the imbued hunters? they have this disturbing trait of...being IMPERVIOUS to mental effects... is it better to try weaponizing random losers with shotguns?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T15:28:25-08:00","id":759431,"title":"","content":"when it comes to imbueds...well..they are wayy to much of a wild card. Can you manipulate them? you can try (by that i dont mean supernatural influence).<br /> <br /> but usually, the Imbued have some ways to tell if they are being used. I would highly recommend to &quot;RUN AWAY!!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T17:07:59-08:00","id":759543,"title":"","content":"I kind of anticipate that any attempt to pull wholescale subversion on the Imbued might end up very badly for the instigators. Just like what happened to the various monsters that breached hunter-net after the Messengers got through with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T18:02:34-08:00","id":759590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/759423-how-to-weaponize-the-imbued?p=759543#post759543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of anticipate that any attempt to pull wholescale subversion on the Imbued might end up very badly for the instigators. Just like what happened to the various monsters that breached hunter-net after the Messengers got through with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell me more, that sounds fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T18:19:30-08:00","id":759604,"title":"","content":"For some reason i can't quite put my finger on, when i first read the title i thought of weaponizing the Created, prometheans, the frankensteinian supernaturals from nWoD, funny that.<br /> <br /> Weaponizing the Imbued? Simpler than people think - false facts can be sincerely told as truth by manipulated or plain brainwashed 3rd parties. The Imbued may try, but do not exist in a vacuum where they only interact with their own and the monsters, quite the opposite possibly. It's a matter of finding one and researching it and who it interacts with bit by bit. Risks certainly exist but wouldn't say they are any greater than in manipulating any supernaturals, be they your own kind or others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T19:50:34-08:00","id":759655,"title":"","content":"If you want to weaponize the Imbued, best do it from as far away as possible. First because they are immune to all mental influence that isn't strictly of the natural variety, but even more than that, because despite Hunter: the Reckoning <i>portraying</i> itself as a nigh-hopeless battle against utterly insurmountable supernatural threats that, despite your Imbued gifts, you could never really hope to defeat, the actual <i>game mechanics</i> of the Imbued gifts mean that it's actually pretty easy to create a Hunter who can straight up curbstomp just about any supernatural creature in the World of Darkness if you can get into the same room as it, full stop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T21:36:48-08:00","id":759713,"title":"","content":"The best method is to play the &quot;good&quot; or &quot;repentant&quot; monster, that's willing to sell out its own kind (or actually be such). Maybe the Imbued will kill all your enemies and then turn on you, but that gives you plenty of time to prepare for that. More likely, most of them are dead in the process.<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> <br /> The idea that the mechanics of the Edges make the Imbued unstoppable combat monsters... is pretty hard to back up. That isn't to say they should be taken lightly as threats, but plenty out there can cream them with ease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T00:02:26-08:00","id":759784,"title":"","content":"I think the real threat from the Imbued comes from lack of in character knowledge. These guys seem like a bunch of bedraggled humans. You don't know you can't simply hypnotize one to just going away with a Geas or some such until one of them responds by pulling out a sawed off shot-gun on you loaded with cold iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 11-08-2015, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T00:30:18-08:00","id":759800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/759423-how-to-weaponize-the-imbued?p=759713#post759713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that the mechanics of the Edges make the Imbued unstoppable combat monsters... is pretty hard to back up. That isn't to say they should be taken lightly as threats, but plenty out there can cream them with ease.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have seen Edges broken pretty badly, though I will admit that you have to actually build your character to be able to break them, and that some of the Creeds are far easier to abuse than others. Innocent and Defender can be downright obnoxious even using just the basic book (and only get worse with later sourcebooks and at higher levels of power). Judge and Visionary not so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T04:10:14-08:00","id":759884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/759423-how-to-weaponize-the-imbued?p=759784#post759784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the real threat from the Imbued comes from lack of in character knowledge. These guys seem like a bunch of bedraggled humans. You don't know you can't simply hypnotize in to just going away with a Geas or some such until one of them responds by pulling out a sawed off shot-gun on you loaded with cold iron.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention that the occasional hunter that was immune to Dominate &amp; such has already existed since Masquerade's 1st edition, making identification of the Imbued as something beside as experienced hunters with a few tricks/numina mostly complicated, i would guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T08:43:38-08:00","id":760003,"title":"","content":"fair points just long thought the garou cant embrace or create ghouls like kindred cant create formori like Dancers, so how to supplement their numbers?<br /> <br /> <br /> oh an idea? Whoever the messengers are has some Presence in the umbra...<br /> <br /> And if you can break in and steal or seize control of this or that artifact?<br /> <br /> you can work a backdoor to the imbueds immunity to mind magics... even Directly command them<br /> <br /> thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T09:00:57-08:00","id":760015,"title":"","content":"I think you should think very, very carefully before you take away one of a splat's defining traits. It's generally a bad idea. It also seems a bit lazy - the best way to deal with the Imbued? Through mortal proxies. The vast majority of their powers either have an extremely limited effect or no effect on mortals. Don't try to summon True Ultimate Power to break through their immunity to mind control; have your mortal stooge make them an offer they can't refuse. Don't send ghouls after the Imbued; send the cops. This works especially well if the supernatural faction in question owns the police. Even better if the Imbued in question have turned their homes into survivalist compounds full of lethal booby traps.<br /> <br /> Conversely, if you can get the imbued working for you - and their immunity to mind control will really only stop incredibly lazy efforts to do so - don't send them up against your enemy's Legion of Doom, and do everything you can to keep the police and the Feds the hell away from them. Pit them instead against the thing they are actually good at fighting and their powers actually work against: Supernatural threats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T09:27:19-08:00","id":760031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/759423-how-to-weaponize-the-imbued?p=759800#post759800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have seen Edges broken pretty badly, though I will admit that you have to actually build your character to be able to break them, and that some of the Creeds are far easier to abuse than others. Innocent and Defender can be downright obnoxious even using just the basic book (and only get worse with later sourcebooks and at higher levels of power). Judge and Visionary not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never seen this actually work out in play. I've seen a lot of people white-room argue it on forums (often ignoring lots of things like the scarcity of Conviction, the difficulty of increasing Virtues, the drawbacks of high Virtues, ignoring that certain Edges are noted as incompatible with each other, etc.), but never sufficiently backed up.<br /> <br /> The fact that you singled out the Innocents and Defenders actually illustrates another problem with these sorts of things: those are only really powerful against stupid monsters. Are Edges like Radiate and Ward vicious against a group of mindless zombies? Yes. Because they're defensive powers. The zombies just sit there flailing idiotically. Anything with a functional brain, on the other hand, can still deal with it. Radiate is (pun intended) blindingly obvious, but you can attack anyone the Innocent couldn't protect normally, or just retreat and ambush the Imbued another time now that they're revealed they're capable of obvious effects. The Defender's Ward might stop you from closing in (though using it in a tight space can cause it to autofail), but you can still just shoot them from outside the edges of it.<br /> <br /> A more general issue, is that Hunters have no Initiative boosters. So things like Celerity, Spirit of the Fray, etc. can easily ensure a dead Hunter before that Hunter can whip out an Edge regardless of if the Edge is broken or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T12:15:55-08:00","id":760137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/759423-how-to-weaponize-the-imbued?p=760031#post760031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never seen this actually work out in play. I've seen a lot of people white-room argue it on forums (often ignoring lots of things like the scarcity of Conviction, the difficulty of increasing Virtues, the drawbacks of high Virtues, ignoring that certain Edges are noted as incompatible with each other, etc.), but never sufficiently backed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is possible that my perspective is somewhat warped and my experience not representative. My experience here comes from playing in a Hunter game with a group of experienced Shadowrun players who had been playing together for a long time (I was new). I played a Redeemer, and wound up being the least useful party member. The other PCs were a Judge, a Visionary, a Defender, and an Innocent. And yeah, they played their characters more or less as experienced Shadowrunners even in the WoD. Pretty much the only time we were ever actually in danger was when we were taken by surprise, which was rare on account of good planning and good recon. And we learned to hate Celerity. That one discipline was the primary reason why our Judge took the ability to render supernatural creatures unable to use abilities that required the use of a supernatural resource (vitae, quintessence, etc) or to spend said supernatural resource for the duration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A more general issue, is that Hunters have no Initiative boosters. So things like Celerity, Spirit of the Fray, etc. can easily ensure a dead Hunter before that Hunter can whip out an Edge regardless of if the Edge is broken or not. </div> </div> </div>This is true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T13:29:59-08:00","id":760173,"title":"","content":"Would the SAD Be better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T15:15:08-08:00","id":760254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/759423-how-to-weaponize-the-imbued?p=760173#post760173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the SAD Be better?</div> </div> </div> </div>Better for what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T16:27:47-08:00","id":760325,"title":"","content":"For trying to weaponize? or Manipulate<br /> <br /> its allready heavily infiltrated... by the GArou...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T18:02:32-08:00","id":760377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/759423-how-to-weaponize-the-imbued?p=760325#post760325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For trying to weaponize? or Manipulate<br /> <br /> its allready heavily infiltrated... by the GArou...</div> </div> </div> </div>It had one Silver Fang kin in it back in the day, who has since been reassigned given that the SAD got pulled apart (see The Hunter's Hunted II).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T17:44:39-08:00","id":761073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/759423-how-to-weaponize-the-imbued?p=760003#post760003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh an idea? Whoever the messengers are has some Presence in the umbra...<br /> <br /> And if you can break in and steal or seize control of this or that artifact?<br /> <br /> you can work a backdoor to the imbueds immunity to mind magics... even Directly command them<br /> <br /> thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would imagine that attempting to suborn the connection the Messengers have with imbued hunters would be a task for supernaturals with an up-to-date last will &amp; testament. Unlike the Incarnae/Celestines, Antediluvians, Oracles, Lady of Fate, Horus, or whatever other nigh-omniscient/omnipotent NPCs are vaguely and distantly involved in motivating PC splats, they take a direct hand in telling their minions who/what to kill and where to find them, and are apparently capable of making more at will anywhere in the world. I'm frankly skeptical that any player character group of whatever type would be able to make the first move toward usurping control of the hunters <i>en masse</i> without the Messengers becoming instantly aware and going to Defcon One.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T21:31:14-08:00","id":761225,"title":"","content":"Well....<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Two groups have a chance, depending which books and hints you go by. If you go with the Messegeners serving the Ministers, then the Kuei-jin have a potential to use their connection to the Ministers to get at the Messengers to manipulate them. If you go with the idea that Lucifer is more responsible for reactivating the Imbued as part of his bid to take out the Earthbound, then demons have the ability to mess with the Messengers as well. These theories aren't mutually exclusive either.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T23:03:16-08:00","id":768984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> 